# Overlay and chip UI

Do not use a full-width inverted header for menus or transients.

**Selection overlay** (MODE, BAND, STEP, VOL, BW, BFO): one 16 px row.

```
TITLE ............... [VALUE]
```

**Font roles**

- **14×24** seven-seg: frequency only (hero). Do not replace with 6×8. Glyph is 14 px; **2 px gap** between cells (1 px if 8 digits would overflow). Packed `kFreqW` blit is off — unreadable.
- **8×16** Pixel Operator: idle chips, overlay TITLE / focus, S-meter `S9+` (same 16 px row as the cubes).
- **Karat 5×7**: MHz, STEREO, small secondary / RDS / service marks. Not the S-meter label — 5×7 cannot fill the 16 px cubes.

- Title: normal 8×16, left.
- Leader dots between title and chip.
- Value: rounded inverted chip (`oledPrintModeBadge`, `paintTransient`).
- Chip fill is **+3 px** after the last glyph and **+3 px** before the first (`BADGE_PAD`). Same for idle chips.
- Encoder changes the chip; confirm with encoder click where the radio would otherwise blink (MODE). STEP also waits for confirm (no timeout).

**Idle chips** (black on filled rounded rect):

- Mode AM/LSB/USB/CW/WFM: top-left. Two-letter labels centered in the chip (`WFM` is three letters).
- Filter width: top-center on SW **and** WFM (`AUTO`, `110k`, `3.0k`, CW `0.5k`). Not plain text.
- WFM stereo: hidden until a stereo pilot. Then a filled 10 px circle after the last S-meter cell; after 2 s of stable stereo it heartbeats (1 s on / 1 s off, 2 s period). Only on the S-meter, only WFM. Not beside the 7-seg. `MHz` is 5×7 on the bottom page of the frequency. Idle mode chip on FM is `WFM`.
- BAND overlay FM tag is `WFM`, CB is `CB`. No band tag on idle.

Do not add idle VOL, kHz on SW, or idle BFO `+    0`. VOL/BFO only in overlay when adjusting.

New settings and transients must use this pattern, not a new menu chrome.
